{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3c3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae11-990a-7e72-a802-0a0580c41ec6"},"sequence":60,"recorded_at":1780531400000115,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae11cd007204b098653072b91cec","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-3k3e6m/TASK-260830-3k3e6m_reviewer-cr1.md`.\n1|Independently review Change Request revision 1 of TASK-260830-3k3e6m (implement-durable-operation-journal, second leaf of STORY-260830-2rqigd workspace-checkpoints-and-operation-journal after the checkpointed 14yo67 sessckpt leaf; sibling 17ootk crash-boundary fault tests follows; task_delta on the Story branch (trunk base 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e; checkpointed predecessors d805720 ; tip d805720ef2d0f862573018f2f5967a1b6c1dc628), published by RUN-260917-1e66fc on muse-spark max, 19 changed paths, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-3k3e6m_change-request_rev1.patch / _rev1-validation.log). Read the producer brief TASK-260830-3k3e6m_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-3k3e6m_results.md, TASK-260830-3k3e6m_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260830-3k3e6m_producer-evidence.tar.gz (logs/, mutant-harness.log), internal/matjournal/TRACEABILITY.md in the candidate, the 14yo67 verdict TASK-260830-14yo67_review-verdict-rev1.md (its Story-close items this leaf carries: section:5.4 registry re-pin, README sessckpt section, forged-Admit negative), the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. The normative authority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md Sections 10.5, 10.6, 13.12, 13.13.\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments: (1) Section 10.6 shape and phases — extract the journal table, the Provider Journal Transaction and Task-board Journal Transaction closed objects, the token nullability rules and the phase enum from the pinned text yourself and diff them against journal.go/marker.go; derive the legal phase transitions from the pinned coordinator order and abort rules independently of the producer's table and compare edge by edge (every edge the producer admits must be grounded in a clause; every edge the text forbids must be refused — plant staging->committed, prepared->committed without committing, rolled_back->anything, committed->rolling_back); check the bridge sub-state table the same way (import/open/adopt/resume/dormant_finalized/rolled_back with the token/ref/expiry nullability per state); confirm the four bridge operation IDs and prepare_operation_id/prepare_request_digest survive reopen and that a retry with byte-unequal body refuses while a byte-equal retry replays without a second effect (assert the file set and inodes). (2) Recovery evaluator — for each CR-MAT-01..08 boundary rerun the producer's crash tests twice, then inject your own crashes with the hooks (blob-without-receipt, receipt-without-journal, torn journal, marker present with journal missing, unknown provider probe at CR-MAT-05..07) and assert Recover selects exactly one of safe_retry | explicit_rollback | recoverable_parked_state with the evidence record fields the gate requires (boundary ID, path, operation IDs, pre/post durable facts, external effect + status probe, winning lease before/after, native identity/binding before/after, outcome); attack exclusivity: construct evidence that satisfies both a retry and a rollback predicate and confirm the evaluator fails closed to parked; confirm the rejection rules (two live authorities, unfenced continuation, new-session launch/fresh handle/relabelled blank state/different realm) are refused as recovery outcomes; confirm parked evidence is durable and re-read byte-identical after reopen. (3) Section 13.12 rows — for each journal-observable row (disk full, atomic rename blocked, owner-resume response lost, operator interrupt, task-board import/open/adopt failures before/after the new lease) drive the producer's TestRecoverFailureMatrixRows and add one row-specific plant of your own. (4) Receipt reconciliation — the sessckpt operation receipt and the journal's prepare receipt are documented as distinct records: judge whether the pinned text supports two receipt shapes or requires one (cite the clause) and whether the sessckpt discipline was reused rather than forked. (5) Refusal census and mutation — enumerate every refuse arm of journal.go/store.go/recover.go/marker.go; each needs a named test reaching it through the production entry (the producer claims 11 narrowing mutants for 11 gates — check that the denominator is the gate count, not the arm count, and report arms without a mutant); rerun mutant_harness.py in an isolated copy, rerun each KILLED twice, plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on arms the producer did not mutate (an exclusivity check dropped in Recover; a nullability rule for open_token in dormant_finalized; the 65536 map bound off by one; a prepare_request_digest compare by prefix) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (6) Story-close items — the forged-Admit same-epoch foreign-lease negative in sessckpt is present and RED under a plant that admits it; README sections for sessckpt and matjournal with test commands and no capability claim; the ownership registry changes (section:5.4 rebound to sessckpt.Capture, new 10.6/13.12/13.13 bindings — 13.12 marked unmeasured because the scanner finds no clause lines in a table-shaped section: judge whether \"unmeasured\" is honest or a gap that must say so), the projection digest re-pinned: recompute it independently, confirm every claimed clause line exists, no self-minted claim, tracecheck 17/489 reproduced. (7) Bounds and hygiene — canonicaljson still refuses materialization-journal 2.0.0 (the shape validates inside matjournal): confirm no consumer treats the canonicaljson refusal as support and that the census pin is honest; last_error at Structured Error 1.2.0 is justified by the pinned registration table; changed_paths exactly the candidate paths, no __pycache__/.pyc, no task-board.config.json, no stray plants; gofmt/vet clean; go test ./internal/matjournal ./internal/sessckpt ./internal/traceability/... -count=1 and -race green; tracecheck and cataloggen -check exit 0 on the exact tree.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-3k3e6m/ and delete candidate copies when done. Attach TASK-260830-3k3e6m_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260830-3k3e6m_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-3k3e6m, revision=1, evidence=TASK-260830-3k3e6m_review-verdict-rev1.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named. Model: muse-spark xhigh (codex reviewers are out of quota until 2026-09-19). Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
