{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c557","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae11-990a-7e72-a802-0a0580c41ec6"},"sequence":262,"recorded_at":1780531400000519,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae12-938d-7c60-a182-438aad20623c"},"task_id":"01a0ae12-938d-7c60-a182-438aad20623c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae12-938d-7c60-a182-438aad20623c","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev3k3e6m/TASK-260830-3k3e6m_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-3k3e6m results: implement-durable-operation-journal\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review. The candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the\n4|managed Story worktree for the handoff to snapshot.\n5|\n6|## Outcome\n7|\n8|`internal/matjournal` implements the Section 10.6 Materialization\n9|Journal 2.0.0 recovery contract: prepare-bound IDs and canonical\n10|request digests, the phase machine with token/bridge/authority rules,\n11|the no-replace prepare receipt, the managed-replica marker validator\n12|and destination classifier, and the status-first `Recover` evaluator\n13|that classifies every CR-MAT-01..08 boundary into exactly one Section\n14|13.13 outcome with durable parked and rollback evidence.\n15|\n16|## AC coverage: 12 of 12 rows driven\n17|\n18|Every row is driven through the named production entry by a named\n19|committed test.\n20|\n21|| # | AC row | Production call site | Test |\n22||---|---|---|---|\n23|| 1 | Journal document created, read, transitioned, persisted | `Store.Create`, `Store.Get`, `Store.Transition` (`internal/matjournal/store.go`) | `TestCreatePersistsJournalAndReceipt`, `TestSpecExampleShapeDrivesThroughProduction` |\n24|| 2 | Operation receipts persisted with ID binding | `Store.Create` receipt install (`store.go`) | `TestCreatePersistsJournalAndReceipt`, `TestCrashBetweenJournalAndReceiptReplays` |\n25|| 3 | Phase transitions enforced | `Store.Transition` (`store.go`, `journal.go`) | `TestTransitionRefusesIllegalEdges`, `TestTransitionGuards`, `TestFullDormantWalkCommits` |\n26|| 4 | Idempotency input digests; byte-unequal retry refuses | `Store.Create` (`replayCreateLocked`) | `TestCreateReplayAndConflict` |\n27|| 5 | Status-first recovery classification | `Store.Recover` (`internal/matjournal/recover.go`) | `TestRecoverGatesPark`, `TestRecoverResumes`, `TestCrash*` |\n28|| 6 | Parked/rollback outcomes durable with lease, IDs, identity, error | `Store.Recover` (`park`, `completeRollback`), `Store.Rollback` | `TestParkedEvidenceIsDurable`, `TestRecoverRollbackRequired`, `TestRollbackConverges` |\n29|| 7 | Exact contract fixtures pass | `Update*`, `Transition`, `ValidateMarker`, `Recover` | `TestSpecExampleShapeDrivesThroughProduction`, `TestOpenedFixtureMatchesProduction`, `TestMarkerExampleValidates`, `TestClassifyDestination`, `TestRecoverFailureMatrixRows` |\n30|| 8 | Negative/refusal cases pass | gates in `journal.go`, `store.go`, `recover.go` | `TestCreateRefusesMalformedClosure`, `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules`, `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals`, `TestAuthorityGuards`, `TestTerminalFreezes`, `TestGetRefusals`, `TestRecoverRefusesBadBoundary` |\n31|| 9 | Crash/idempotency evidence | hooks + `Recover` | 8 `TestCrash*` boundaries with hook crashes + reopen + `Recover`, `TestCreateCrashChildSelfTerminates` (real SIGKILL), replay tests |\n32|| 10 | No unsupported capability advertised | (no CLI/doctor/claim surface) | `cigate` capability-claim gate green; README sections use the no-claim closer |\n33|| 11 | Receipt reconciliation | prepare receipt adopts the sessckpt discipline; distinct record documented | `internal/matjournal/TRACEABILITY.md` (Receipt reconciliation) |\n34|| 12 | Story-close items: forged-Admit negative, README sections, ownership bindings + re-pin | `sessckpt.Admit`, README, `ownership.v0.6.0.json` | `TestAdmitRefusesSameEpochForeignLeaseHead`, `TestREADMEOwnershipFiguresAreDerivedFromTheMeasuredReport`, `tracecheck` |\n35|\n36|## Gating behavior and killers\n37|\n38|Every refusing gate ships a narrowing mutant (gate stays present,\n39|weakened to admit exactly one member of the rejected class) plus the\n40|named killer. Full battery: `python3\n41|internal/matjournal/mutant_harness.py` — 11 KILLED, 1 control\n42|SURVIVED, exit 0 (log: `logs/mutant-harness.log`).\n43|\n44|| Gate (production site) | Mutant | Killer |\n45||---|---|---|\n46|| Phase table (`legalTransitions`) | N-phase-table (admits staging-to-committed; literals preserved) | `TestTransitionRefusesIllegalEdges` |\n47|| Bridge sub-table (`boardTransitions`) | N-board-subtable (admits not_started-to-opened; literals preserved) | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/subtable_refuses_skip` |\n48|| Provider token rule (`checkProviderTransaction`) | N-provider-token (admits prepared-without-token) | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules/prepared_requires_token` |\n49|| Import triple (`requireImportTriple`) | N-board-import (admits expiry-less imports) | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/imported_triple_incomplete` |\n50|| Bridge ID drift (`checkTaskBoardDrift`) | N-id-drift-adopt (admits adopt-ID drift) | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/operation_drift_refuses` |\n51|| First-prepare conflict (`replayCreateLocked`) | N-create-first-prepare (admits different-operation same-body replay) | `TestCreateReplayAndConflict` |\n52|| Pre-activation (`checkPreActivation`) | N-rollback-adopt (admits adopted rollback) | `TestTransitionGuards/rollback_refused_after_adopt` |\n53|| Failed evidence (`checkTransitionGuards`) | N-failed-null (admits explicit-null error) | `TestTransitionGuards/failed_requires_error` |\n54|| Commit marker (`checkTransitionGuards`) | N-commit-marker (admits marker-less commits with authorities) | `TestTransitionGuards/committed_workspace_requires_marker` |\n55|| Crash-window uncertainty (`providerEffectUncertain`) | N-recover-uncertain-floor (admits CR-MAT-05..07 unknown probes) | `TestParkedEvidenceIsDurable` |\n56|| Token grammar (`checkToken`) | N-token-length (admits exactly 3-byte tokens) | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules/short_token_refuses` |\n57|\n58|No gate inspects source text: every gate is a value, table, or grammar\n59|comparison, so the token-preserving requirement holds structurally via\n60|the table mutants. The byte-equality and digest checks are redundant\n61|defenses (either refuses a moved body alone), so the idempotency\n62|mutant targets the first-prepare check with a message-specific killer.\n63|\n64|## Validation (all exit 0)\n65|\n66|- `go test ./... -count=1`: 28 packages ok (`logs/suite.log`)\n67|- `go test ./internal/matjournal/ -count=1 -v` (`logs/matjournal-tests.log`), `-cover`: 77.0%\n68|- `go test ./internal/sessckpt/ -count=1` (`logs/sessckpt-tests.log`), `-cover`: 82.1%\n69|- `go vet ./...`, `go build ./...`, `GOOS=windows go build ./...`, `gofmt -l` clean (`logs/gates.log`)\n70|- Catalog `-check` and `tracecheck` pass: acceptance_cases=105, bindings=59, clauses 17/489 (`logs/gates.log`)\n71|\n72|## Files changed (uncommitted in the Story worktree)\n73|\n74|- `internal/matjournal/`: `doc.go`, `journal.go`, `marker.go`, `store.go`, `recover.go`, `journal_test.go`, `refusal_test.go`, `recover_test.go`, `crash_test.go`, `crash_unix_test.go`, `mutant_harness.py`, `TRACEABILITY.md` (new package)\n75|- `internal/sessckpt/refusal_test.go`: `TestAdmitRefusesSameEpochForeignLeaseHead` (verdict section 4)\n76|- `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json`: 4 acceptance cases; section:5.4 rebound to `sessckpt.Capture`; new section:10.6, 13.12 (unmeasured: the scanner finds no clause line in the table-shaped section), 13.13 bindings\n77|- `internal/traceability/traceability.go`: re-pinned `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` to the reviewed projection\n78|- `internal/traceability/traceability_test.go`, `internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`: measured counts\n79|- `README.md`: Workspace Checkpoint Records + Materialization Journal sections; ownership figures 101/56 to 105/59\n80|- `LOGBOOK.md`: task entry\n81|\n82|## Stated bounds\n83|\n84|- Journal/marker shapes validate in `matjournal`; the canonicaljson\n85|  shape owner still refuses `materialization-journal` 2.0.0 and its\n86|  census pins that registration. Replacing it is outside this leaf.\n87|- The plan is an opaque digest input; only its authority routing view\n88|  is cross-checked. Operation-predecessor and prior-classification\n89|  rules stay with the plan owner.\n90|- Provider/bridge/marker/lease/native states are modeled `Recover`\n91|  inputs; staging removal and predecessor restoration are coordinator\n92|  work; marker files belong to the replica owner.\n93|- last_error encodes Structured Error 1.2.0, the earliest version\n94|  registering every emitted code (`operation_uncertain` registers at\n95|  1.2.0, not below).\n96|- The phase and sub-state tables derive from the coordinator order,\n97|  fixtures, and abort rules; each derived edge is documented in\n98|  `TRACEABILITY.md` and the code comments name their grounding.","final_result":true}}}
