{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae11-990a-7e72-a802-0a0580c41ec6"},"sequence":264,"recorded_at":1780531400000523,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae12-93d1-74f2-a1ba-7c4028a070c7"},"task_id":"01a0ae12-93d1-74f2-a1ba-7c4028a070c7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae12-93d1-74f2-a1ba-7c4028a070c7","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev3k3e6m/TASK-260830-3k3e6m_conformance-matrix.md`.\n1|# Materialization Journal Traceability\n2|\n3|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, Section 10.6\n4|(Materialization Journal), Section 10.5 (Materialization Plan,\n5|referenced immutable input), Section 13.12 (failure matrix), and\n6|Section 13.13 (crash/restart outcome gate). The task scope cites the\n7|same section numbers of v0.5.0; the headings are retained in v0.6.0.\n8|\n9|## Production entries\n10|\n11|| Entry | File | Behavior |\n12||---|---|---|\n13|| `Open` | `store.go` | Binds the owner-only materializations root; the root must be absolute. |\n14|| `Create` | `store.go` | Binds both caller-stable IDs and the canonical request digest before any staging or bridge mutation; installs plan view, journal, and prepare receipt; byte-identical retries replay, moved bodies conflict. |\n15|| `Get` | `store.go` | Returns byte-identical journal bytes, re-validated through the closed shape on every read. |\n16|| `UpdateProvider` | `store.go` | Records one provider transaction state with the token rule and ID binding. |\n17|| `UpdateTaskBoard` | `store.go` | Records one task-board state along the sub-state table with the nullability rules and bridge-key binding. |\n18|| `UpdateAuthority` | `store.go` | Records one authority state along the sub-state table with the rollback-root rules. |\n19|| `RecordProgress` | `store.go` | Merges per-blob chunk sets and whole-blob verifications in staging or validating. |\n20|| `RecordError` | `store.go` | Records the redacted Structured Error without moving the phase. |\n21|| `Transition` | `store.go` | Moves the phase along the table with the entry guards. |\n22|| `Rollback` | `store.go` | Executes the allowed abort: rolling_back first, then converged rolled_back. |\n23|| `Recover` | `recover.go` | Classifies one crashed materialization into exactly one Section 13.13 outcome, executing rollback or provable completions. |\n24|| `ValidateMarker` | `marker.go` | Validates the closed marker shape and attests the omit-self identity. |\n25|| `ClassifyDestination` | `marker.go` | Classifies one destination from its durable facts. |\n26|\n27|## Conformance matrix\n28|\n29|`n of m AC rows driven`: every row below is driven through the named\n30|production entry by the named committed test.\n31|\n32|### Journal shape and prepare (Section 10.6)\n33|\n34|| Spec row | Production | Test |\n35||---|---|---|\n36|| Journal closed 22-member shape, literals, null legs | `Create`, `Get` (`store.go`, `journal.go`) | `TestCreatePersistsJournalAndReceipt` |\n37|| Normative prepared example members | `UpdateProvider`, `UpdateAuthority`, `UpdateTaskBoard`, `Transition` | `TestSpecExampleShapeDrivesThroughProduction` |\n38|| MJ-TASK-BOARD-OPENED-POS verbatim fixture | `UpdateTaskBoard` | `TestOpenedFixtureMatchesProduction` |\n39|| Import/open/adopt/resume operation-ID allocation with the materialization ID; no second manager | `Create` | `TestCreatePersistsJournalAndReceipt`, `TestCreateReplayAndConflict` |\n40|| Same IDs plus byte-identical body replay; moved body refuses idempotency_mismatch (MJ-RPC-PREPARE-LOST) | `Create` (`replayCreateLocked`) | `TestCreateReplayAndConflict` |\n41|| Second prepare for one materialization refuses | `Create` | `TestCreateReplayAndConflict` |\n42|| Malformed closure members refuse the invalid class | `Create` (`buildCreate`) | `TestCreateRefusesMalformedClosure` |\n43|| Unknown/absent journal and torn bytes | `Get` | `TestGetRefusals` |\n44|\n45|### Phase machine (Section 10.6, derived table)\n46|\n47|The pinned text names the phase enum and the coordinator order but no\n48|explicit edge table; the table in `legalTransitions` derives one edge\n49|per order step (prepare creates staging, transfer stages, validation\n50|validates, commit returns prepared, finalize commits), one abort edge\n51|per non-terminal phase (a valid staging transaction resumes or rolls\n52|back), and one failure edge per non-terminal phase. The\n53|committing-to-rolling_back edge additionally requires pre-activation\n54|(byte rollback is forbidden after adopt). Each edge is proved by the\n55|walk tests and the full illegal-pair battery.\n56|\n57|| Spec row | Production | Test |\n58||---|---|---|\n59|| Every legal edge admits | `Transition` | `TestSpecExampleShapeDrivesThroughProduction`, `TestFullDormantWalkCommits`, `TestRollbackConverges` |\n60|| Every illegal pair refuses with the table message | `Transition` | `TestTransitionRefusesIllegalEdges` |\n61|| Prepared requires provider prepared and opened bridge durable | `Transition` (`checkTransitionGuards`) | `TestTransitionGuards/prepared_requires_opened`, `prepared_requires_provider_prepared` |\n62|| Committed requires converged sub-states, resumed/dormant bridge, authorities committed, exact destination marker for workspace | `Transition` | `TestTransitionGuards/committed_requires_convergence`, `committed_workspace_requires_marker`, `committed_rejects_drifting_marker` |\n63|| Failed requires the explaining last_error | `Transition` | `TestTransitionGuards/failed_requires_error`, `TestLastErrorIsRedactedStructuredError` |\n64|| Terminal phases freeze every entry | `update` | `TestTerminalFreezes`, `TestTransitionRefusesIllegalEdges` |\n65|\n66|### Provider, bridge, authority rules (Sections 10.6, 7.5)\n67|\n68|| Spec row | Production | Test |\n69||---|---|---|\n70|| Prepared requires a token; every other state requires null | `UpdateProvider` | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules` |\n71|| Token base64url-256+ grammar (fixpoint, 32..512 bytes) | `checkToken` | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules`, `TestTokenFixturesAreWellFormed` |\n72|| Transaction authority closed shape and mat/tx/plan binding | `UpdateProvider` | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules/authority_ids_bind` |\n73|| Transaction ID stable; per-call operation ID may advance | `UpdateProvider` | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules/transaction_drift_refuses`, `operation_id_may_advance` |\n74|| Bridge null/state invariants per state | `UpdateTaskBoard` | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals` |\n75|| Bridge sub-state table incl. no adopted rollback | `UpdateTaskBoard` | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/subtable_*` |\n76|| Dormant cleanup_after equals the consumed open expiry | `UpdateTaskBoard` | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/dormant_expiry_binds_consumed`, `TestFullDormantWalkCommits` |\n77|| Failed preserves only one still-valid pair | `UpdateTaskBoard` | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/failed_*` |\n78|| Bridge operation-ID drift refuses | `UpdateTaskBoard` (`checkTaskBoardDrift`) | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/operation_drift_refuses` |\n79|| Authority sub-table, rollback-root rules, single provider backup | `UpdateAuthority` | `TestAuthorityGuards` |\n80|| Per-blob chunk sets merge by union (MJ-MULTIBLOB-POS) | `RecordProgress` | `TestRecordProgressMergesPerBlob` |\n81|| Progress closes after validation | `RecordProgress` | `TestRecordProgressMergesPerBlob` |\n82|| Rollback converges tokens, states, and the terminal failure; refuses past activation and without a failure | `Rollback` | `TestRollbackConverges`, `TestTransitionGuards/rollback_refused_*` |\n83|\n84|### Marker and destination (Section 10.6)\n85|\n86|| Spec row | Production | Test |\n87||---|---|---|\n88|| Normative marker example validates; marker_id recomputes | `ValidateMarker` | `TestMarkerExampleValidates` |\n89|| Marker binding (replica, plan, checkpoint, materialization, predecessor) | `Transition`, `Recover` (`checkMarkerBinding`) | `TestTransitionGuards/committed_rejects_drifting_marker`, `TestRecoverCompletesCommit` |\n90|| Destination classes incl. MARKER-* rows | `ClassifyDestination` | `TestClassifyDestination` |\n91|\n92|### Recovery (Sections 13.12, 13.13)\n93|\n94|| Spec row | Production | Test |\n95||---|---|---|\n96|| CR-MAT-01..08, each with a real crash injection followed by `Recover` | `Recover` | `TestCrash*` (8 boundaries), `TestCreateCrashChildSelfTerminates` (SIGKILL) |\n97|| MJ-CRASH-STAGE/PREPARE-LOST/COMMIT-LOST/ROLLBACK-LOST/MARKER-MISMATCH | `Recover` | `TestCrashAfterTransferResumes`, `TestCrashAfterProviderPreparePersistsToken`, `TestRecoverResumes/committing_retries_commit`, `TestRecoverCompletesCommit`, `TestRecoverRollbackRequired`, `TestRecoverGatesPark/marker_mismatch` |\n98|| TB-TXN IMPORT/OPEN/ADOPT/RESUME-LOST, BINDING-MISMATCH, TOKEN-EXPIRED, PASSIVE | `Recover` | `TestRecoverResumes/bridge_*`, `TestRecoverGatesPark/binding_mismatch`, `TestRecoverRollbackRequired/token_expired_before_lease`, `TestFullDormantWalkCommits`, `TestRecoverCompletesCommit/dormant_finalize_closes` |\n99|| 13.12 disk full / rename blocked park with remediation | `Recover` | `TestRecoverGatesPark/disk_full`, `rename_blocked` |\n100|| 13.12 owner-resume lost finalizes under the same IDs | `Recover` | `TestRecoverFailureMatrixRows/owner_resume_lost_finalizes` |\n101|| 13.12 operator interrupt retries the same operation | `Recover` | `TestRecoverFailureMatrixRows/operator_interrupt_retries_same_operation` |\n102|| 13.12 import/open/adopt fail before the lease rolls back | `Recover` | `TestRecoverRollbackRequired/bridge_failed_before_lease`, `token_expired_before_lease` |\n103|| 13.12 adopt fails after the lease stays the stopped owner | `Recover` | `TestRecoverFailureMatrixRows/adopt_fails_after_lease_stays_stopped_owner` |\n104|| Rejection gates: moved/unknown lease, substitution, two live authorities, unfenced continuation, marker integrity, unknown decisive status, token/binding contradiction, torn progression | `Recover` | `TestRecoverGatesPark`, `TestRecoverTornJournalParks`, `TestRecoverContradictoryProgressionParks` |\n105|| Terminal journals replay; park leaves them frozen | `Recover` | `TestRecoverTerminalReplays` |\n106|| Parked/rollback evidence durable with lease, IDs, identity, error; never a fourth outcome | `Recover` (`park`, `completeRollback`) | `TestParkedEvidenceIsDurable`, `mustOutcome` (every recovery test) |\n107|\n108|## Mutants\n109|\n110|Run: `python3 internal/matjournal/mutant_harness.py`. All narrowing\n111|mutants are KILLED; the harmless control SURVIVES. No gate inspects\n112|source text: every gate is a value, table, or grammar comparison, so\n113|the token-preserving requirement holds structurally — the table\n114|mutants (N-phase-table, N-board-subtable) preserve every literal and\n115|change only the edge set.\n116|\n117|| Mutant | Weakening | Killer |\n118||---|---|---|\n119|| N-phase-table | Admits staging-to-committed | `TestTransitionRefusesIllegalEdges` |\n120|| N-board-subtable | Admits not_started-to-opened | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/subtable_refuses_skip` |\n121|| N-provider-token | Admits prepared-without-token | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules/prepared_requires_token` |\n122|| N-board-import | Admits expiry-less imports | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/imported_triple_incomplete` |\n123|| N-id-drift-adopt | Admits adopt-ID drift | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/operation_drift_refuses` |\n124|| N-create-first-prepare | Admits different-operation same-body replay | `TestCreateReplayAndConflict` |\n125|| N-rollback-adopt | Admits adopted rollback | `TestTransitionGuards/rollback_refused_after_adopt` |\n126|| N-failed-null | Admits explicit-null explaining error | `TestTransitionGuards/failed_requires_error` |\n127|| N-commit-marker | Admits marker-less commits on journals with authorities | `TestTransitionGuards/committed_workspace_requires_marker` |\n128|| N-recover-uncertain-floor | Admits unrecorded-prepare unknown probes at CR-MAT-05..07 | `TestParkedEvidenceIsDurable` |\n129|| N-token-length | Admits exactly 3-byte tokens | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules/short_token_refuses` |\n130|| C-doc-comment | Comment-only control | `TestTokenFixturesAreWellFormed` (SURVIVES) |\n131|\n132|## Receipt reconciliation\n133|\n134|The prepare receipt adopts the sessckpt operation-receipt discipline —\n135|an operation-keyed, input-digest-compared, no-replace receipt installed\n136|after the bytes it names — and is a distinct record because it binds\n137|the materialize.prepare namespace (prepare operation, canonical\n138|request body, journal) rather than a checkpoint capture (capture\n139|operation, record bytes, checkpoint). The two receipts are never\n140|interchangeable: different operations, different idempotency keys,\n141|different digests, different result bindings. Sharing one shape would\n142|merge the namespaces the idempotency rules keep apart.\n143|\n144|## Stated bounds\n145|\n146|- The journal and marker shapes validate in this package; the\n147|  canonicaljson owner still registers materialization-journal 2.0.0\n148|  (and materialization-plan 1.0.0) with\n149|  rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape, and its census and inventory\n150|  suites pin that registration. Replacing it is outside this leaf.\n151|- The plan is an opaque digest input; only its authority routing view\n152|  (kind, platform, root path) is cross-checked. Operation-predecessor\n153|  and prior-checkpoint classification rules stay with the plan owner.\n154|- Status probes (provider, bridge, marker, lease, native) are modeled\n155|  inputs. No Mesh RPC, provider plugin, bridge process, or lease\n156|  arbitration is driven here.\n157|- Filesystem staging removal and predecessor restoration are\n158|  coordinator work; the journal records the converged states and the\n159|  probe-verified closure facts.\n160|- Marker history/current files belong to the replica owner; this\n161|  package validates marker bytes and classifies destinations.\n162|- The package adds no `ax` command, no `doctor` result, and no runtime\n163|  capability claim.","final_result":true}}}
