{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5eb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae11-990a-7e72-a802-0a0580c41ec6"},"sequence":336,"recorded_at":1780531400000667,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae12-bed2-7493-b1ab-445dc239eefe"},"task_id":"01a0ae12-bed2-7493-b1ab-445dc239eefe","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae12-bed2-7493-b1ab-445dc239eefe","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-10-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"10\\\\.6\\\\|Materialization Journal\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md | head -20; echo ===; grep -n \\\"^## 13\\\\.12\\\\|^## 13\\\\.13\\\\|^### \\\\|CR-MAT\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md | head -60\",\n  \"description\": \"Locate spec sections in pinned text\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"3083:Materialization Journal is terminal and for at least\\n3298:owner-only Materialization Journal and prepared Provider Transaction Document,\\n5728:### 10.6 Materialization Journal\\n5730:Materialization Journal schema\\n5738:| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Journal schema identifier |\\n6010:| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Journal schema identifier |\\n7407:receiver MUST durably create the Materialization Journal with both IDs and a\\n7444:rollbackable <code>prepared</code> phase and MUST durably write the Section 10.6\\n7450:the durable Section 10.6 bridge IDs and token to adopt, resume, and prove status;\\n7455:a workspace/composite plan it writes the exact Section 10.6 Managed Replica\\n7596:| Materialization Journal and Managed Replica Marker variants | Journal has no content identity; marker ID is machine-local commit evidence | Machine-local recovery state; excluded |\\n7795:per-target atomic renames. The Materialization Journal is the coordinator. A\\n7834:divergent state. Classification MUST use the Section 10.6 current marker and a\\n9316:   the journaled Section 10.6 import/open sequence inside commit, never before\\n10726:Materialization Journal 3.0.0 is a complete clone-only schema and does not\\n15684:| <code>AC-MARKER-001</code> | Absent, matching, content/path-mismatching, replacement, and crash-reconstructed Managed Replica Markers produce the exact classifications, marker identity, atomic current/history writes, and fail-closed recovery in Section 10.6. |\\n15961:| Provider capture, transfer, and rollback | Object Sink plus capture and prepare/status/commit/rollback in Section 7.5, per-blob journal state in Section 10.6, and composite recovery in Sections 11.3 and 13 |\\n15972:| Managed-replica marker had no contract | Closed machine-local marker variant, JCS identity, exact paths, atomic write, classification, migration, replacement, and crash fixtures in Sections 3.2, 10.6, 11.3, and 11.7 |\\n15984:| Provider transactions could not survive fresh plugin processes safely | Sections 3.2 and 7.5 define host-created object-source/transaction authorities, exact durable layout, path disjointness, same-filesystem atomicity, restart lookup/retention, and all-operation authority passing; Section 10.6 journals the authority and Section 11.3 maps every rollback reason; <code>AC-PTX-001</code> covers cross-process recovery |\\n15993:| Task-board materialization lacked durable subtransaction recovery | Section 10.6 defines the exact journaled bridge IDs, tokens, references, state/null rules, order, cleanup, and crash/expiry cases; Section 11.3 exposes token-free status and Sections 13.3/13.6–13.8/13.10 use the same coordinator; <code>AC-TB-004</code> covers all paths |\\n===\\n21:### 1.1 Normative language\\n32:### 1.2 Product boundary\\n75:### 1.3 Conformance targets\\n97:### 1.4 Source authority and evidence\\n113:### 1.5 Normative contract registry\\n224:### 1.6 Common data rules\\n374:### 2.1 Terms\\n404:### 2.2 Global invariants\\n593:### 2.3 Session name resolution\\n626:### 2.4 Execution profiles\\n685:### 3.1 Required components\\n745:### 3.2 Platform paths\\n864:### 3.3 SQLite\\n878:### 4.A TerminalBackend authority and terminology\\n904:### 4.B Registry, identity, discovery, and trust\\n1062:### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\\n1200:### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\\n1289:### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\\n1354:### 4.1 Terminal backend interface\\n1383:### 4.2 tmux backend\\n1430:### 4.3 Native Windows backend\\n1448:### 4.4 User services\\n1471:### 5.1 Session Record\\n1729:### 5.2 Session Event\\n1908:### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\\n1983:### 5.4 Checkpoint Record\\n2085:### 5.5 Provider Identity Record\\n2151:### 5.6 Workspace Group Record\\n2284:### 5.7 Derived session states\\n2343:### 6.1 Loading and precedence\\n2372:### 6.2 Normative example\\n2436:### 6.3 Field constraints\\n2519:### 6.4 Configuration 2.0.0 directory extension\\n2591:### 6.5 Configuration 3.0.0 TerminalBackend extension\\n2636:### 6.6 Configuration 4.0.0 host-channel migration\\n2688:### 7.1 Discovery and trust\\n2720:### 7.2 Framing and lifecycle\\n2811:### 7.3 Provider Manifest\\n2863:### 7.4 Capability result\\n2942:### 7.5 Required operations\\n3461:### 7.6 Quiescence proof\\n3491:### 7.7 Profile mapping\\n3518:### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\\n3553:### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\\n3740:### 7.9 Companion Directory Node protocol\\n3912:### 8.1 Matrix notation\\n3927:### 8.2 Native-store contract matrix\\n3945:### 8.3 Capability matrix\\n3963:### 8.4 Provider/platform matrix\\n4003:### 9.1 Ownership boundary\\n4022:### 9.2 Official bridge command surface\\n4353:### 9.3 Task-board Bundle\\n4617:### 9.4 Local and remote boards\\n4630:### 9.5 Task-board capability reality\\n4647:### 10.1 Record envelope\\n4666:### 10.2 Content-addressed blobs\\n4720:### 10.3 Transfer Chunk Descriptor\\n4748:### 10.4 Transfer Manifest\\n5283:### 10.5 Materialization Plan\\n5728:### 10.6 Materialization Journal\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4941,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1236,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
