{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c669","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae11-990a-7e72-a802-0a0580c41ec6"},"sequence":399,"recorded_at":1780531400000793,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae12-dfdf-7331-8451-ea9ebb09df68"},"task_id":"01a0ae12-dfdf-7331-8451-ea9ebb09df68","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae12-dfdf-7331-8451-ea9ebb09df68","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev3k3e6m/spec106.md`.\n1|### 10.6 Materialization Journal\n2|\n3|Materialization Journal schema\n4|<code>urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal</code> version\n5|<code>2.0.0</code> is a two-variant machine-local recovery contract. Both the\n6|mutable journal and immutable managed-replica marker MUST NOT be replicated.\n7|The journal top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n8|\n9|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n10|| --- | --- | --- |\n11|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Journal schema identifier |\n12|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>2.0.0</code> |\n13|| <code>document_kind</code> | enum | Literal <code>journal</code> |\n14|| <code>materialization_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable across retries |\n15|| <code>prepare_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Caller-stable Mesh RPC prepare idempotency key, allocated with the materialization ID before the first request |\n16|| <code>prepare_request_digest</code> | digest | SHA-256 of the complete canonical <code>materialize.prepare</code> request body, including both caller-stable IDs |\n17|| <code>transfer_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null | Null when all inputs already exist locally |\n18|| <code>plan_id</code> | digest | Exact Materialization Plan |\n19|| <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Validated source checkpoint |\n20|| <code>managed_replica_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null | Non-null when workspace bytes participate |\n21|| <code>authority_states</code> | map(root-id,Authority Journal State)[0..512] | Exactly one entry per plan RootAuthority; empty only for validation-only provider plan |\n22|| <code>expected_prior_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for absent/empty destination |\n23|| <code>completed_blob_chunks</code> | map(digest,sorted unique uint32[0..32768])[0..65536] | Chunk indexes keyed by their Blob ID; sufficient for the maximum file/blob cardinality of one committed transfer closure |\n24|| <code>verified_blob_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..65536] | Whole-blob verification, not chunk presence; sufficient for the maximum file/blob cardinality of one committed transfer closure |\n25|| <code>phase</code> | enum | <code>staging</code>, <code>validating</code>, <code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, <code>rolling_back</code>, <code>rolled_back</code>, <code>committed</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n26|| <code>provider_transaction</code> | Provider Journal Transaction or null | Non-null only when a provider plugin participates |\n27|| <code>task_board_transaction</code> | Task-board Journal Transaction or null | Non-null only when the task-board bridge participates |\n28|| <code>destination_marker_id</code> | digest or null | Managed-replica marker; non-null in committed workspace/composite transactions |\n29|| <code>last_error</code> | Structured Error or null | Redacted exact Section 15.1 object |\n30|| <code>started_at</code> | timestamp | First durable journal write |\n31|| <code>updated_at</code> | timestamp | Latest durable transition, not authority |\n32|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS machine-local extensions only |\n33|\n34|Provider Journal Transaction is a closed object containing exactly\n35|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n36|<code>state:unknown|prepared|committed|rolled_back</code>,\n37|<code>rollback_token:base64url-256+|null</code>,\n38|<code>transaction_authority:ProviderTransactionAuthority</code>, and\n39|<code>last_status_at:timestamp</code>. Prepared requires a non-null token;\n40|every other state requires null. The token and transaction root are\n41|machine-local and MUST be redacted from ordinary logs. The authority's\n42|materialization, provider, transaction, and plan IDs MUST equal the journal and\n43|referenced plan; its root is the only path passed to later plugin processes.\n44|\n45|Task-board Journal Transaction is a closed object containing exactly:\n46|\n47|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n48|| --- | --- | --- |\n49|| <code>bundle_id</code> | digest | Exact Task-board Bundle installed by the plan |\n50|| <code>activation_mode</code> | enum | <code>dormant_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, <code>ownership_transfer</code>, or <code>fork</code> |\n51|| <code>import_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge import key allocated before import |\n52|| <code>open_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge open key allocated before open |\n53|| <code>adopt_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge adopt key allocated before adopt |\n54|| <code>resume_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge resume key allocated before resume |\n55|| <code>state</code> | enum | <code>not_started</code>, <code>imported</code>, <code>opened</code>, <code>adopted</code>, <code>resumed</code>, <code>dormant_finalized</code>, <code>rolled_back</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n56|| <code>import_token</code> | base64url-256+ or null | Owner-only bridge token; non-null exactly in <code>imported</code> and consumed by <code>open</code> |\n57|| <code>staged_manager_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null exactly in <code>imported</code> and consumed by <code>open</code> |\n58|| <code>import_expires_at</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null exactly while import token is usable |\n59|| <code>open_token</code> | base64url-256+ or null | Owner-only bridge token; non-null from opened until adopt or dormant finalization |\n60|| <code>dormant_manager_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null in <code>opened</code> and <code>dormant_finalized</code>; consumed and replaced by <code>manager_session_ref</code> on adopt |\n61|| <code>open_expires_at</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null exactly while open token is usable |\n62|| <code>manager_session_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null after successful adopt |\n63|| <code>ax_binding</code> | Ax Binding or null | Non-null after successful adopt |\n64|| <code>last_bridge_state</code> | enum or null | <code>dormant</code>, <code>quiesced</code>, <code>stopped</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>idle</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n65|| <code>last_status_at</code> | timestamp or null | Time of last bridge status reconciliation |\n66|| <code>cleanup_state</code> | enum | <code>not_started</code>, <code>pending_expiry</code>, <code>retained_active</code>, or <code>removed</code> |\n67|| <code>cleanup_after</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null only for dormant finalized state; copied from the last open expiry |\n68|\n69|Ax Binding is the exact closed bridge shape\n70|<code>{ax_session_id:UUIDv7, lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0, lease_id:UUIDv4}</code>.\n71|The four operation IDs are allocated once with the materialization ID and MUST\n72|survive process restart. A retry MUST use the same operation ID and byte-equal\n73|body. Tokens and manager references are local recovery capabilities: they MUST\n74|be encrypted with the platform credential facility when available, owner-only\n75|at rest otherwise, redacted from ordinary logs, excluded from replication, and\n76|never returned by Mesh RPC.\n77|\n78|The null/state invariants are exact. <code>not_started</code> has all tokens and\n79|references null. <code>imported</code> has import token, staged reference, and\n80|import expiry only. <code>opened</code> has open token, dormant reference, and\n81|open expiry only. <code>adopted</code> and <code>resumed</code> have manager\n82|reference and binding only; their cleanup state is\n83|<code>retained_active</code>. <code>dormant_finalized</code> has dormant\n84|reference only, no usable token, bridge state <code>dormant</code>, and cleanup\n85|state <code>pending_expiry</code> with non-null <code>cleanup_after</code> equal\n86|to the consumed open expiry. Every other state requires\n87|<code>cleanup_after = null</code>. <code>rolled_back</code> has no token or\n88|reference and cleanup state <code>removed</code>. <code>failed</code> preserves\n89|only the still-valid token/reference pair needed for deterministic status or\n90|expiry recovery; <code>last_error</code> explains the failure.\n91|\n92|Authority Journal State is a closed object containing exactly\n93|<code>root_path:absolute-path</code>,\n94|<code>completed_sequences:sorted unique uint53[0..65536]</code>,\n95|<code>observed_prior_digest:digest|null</code>,\n96|<code>rollback_root:absolute-path|null</code>, and\n97|<code>state:staging|prepared|committed|rolled_back</code>. The root path MUST\n98|equal its plan authority; completed sequences contain only operations naming\n99|that authority. Prepared requires a non-null rollback root, committed and\n100|rolled-back require null after cleanup, and staging permits null only before\n101|the first target backup exists. The observed prior digest equals every\n102|non-null operation predecessor for a one-target authority; an authority with\n103|multiple distinct predecessors uses null here and each operation backup stores\n104|its own digest under the rollback root. For a provider-store authority, the\n105|rollback root MUST equal\n106|<code>ProviderTransactionAuthority.root_path/backups/&lt;authority-id&gt;</code>;\n107|the host journal references the plugin backup and MUST NOT allocate a second\n108|provider backup location.\n109|\n110|After a crash, <code>ax</code> MUST resume a valid staging transaction or roll\n111|it back. It MUST NOT guess whether an incomplete commit succeeded; it MUST\n112|reconcile the journal, destination marker, and manifest digest.\n113|\n114|Normative example:\n115|\n116|~~~json\n117|{\n118|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal\",\n119|  \"schema_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n120|  \"document_kind\": \"journal\",\n121|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n122|  \"prepare_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-b180-72cc-9271-1234567890ab\",\n123|  \"prepare_request_digest\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\n124|  \"transfer_id\": \"0198f4c8-d3a0-74bb-9475-1234567890ab\",\n125|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n126|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n127|  \"managed_replica_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-2234567890ab\",\n128|  \"authority_states\": {\n129|    \"codex_sessions\": {\n130|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.codex/sessions\",\n131|      \"completed_sequences\": [2],\n132|      \"observed_prior_digest\": null,\n133|      \"rollback_root\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/provider-transactions/codex/0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab/backups/codex_sessions\",\n134|      \"state\": \"prepared\"\n135|    },\n136|    \"workspace_relux\": {\n137|      \"root_path\": \"/srv/relux\",\n138|      \"completed_sequences\": [1],\n139|      \"observed_prior_digest\": \"sha256:3333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333\",\n140|      \"rollback_root\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/materializations/0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab/workspace_relux\",\n141|      \"state\": \"prepared\"\n142|    }\n143|  },\n144|  \"expected_prior_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:2222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222\",\n145|  \"completed_blob_chunks\": {\n146|    \"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\": [0],\n147|    \"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\": [0]\n148|  },\n149|  \"verified_blob_ids\": [\n150|    \"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\",\n151|    \"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\"\n152|  ],\n153|  \"phase\": \"prepared\",\n154|  \"provider_transaction\": {\n155|    \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n156|    \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n157|    \"state\": \"prepared\",\n158|    \"rollback_token\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXowMTIzNDU2Nzg5QUI\",\n159|    \"transaction_authority\": {\n160|      \"authority_id\": \"provider_transaction\",\n161|      \"kind\": \"provider_transaction\",\n162|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/provider-transactions/codex/0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n163|      \"layout\": \"provider_transaction_v1\",\n164|      \"access\": \"read_write\",\n165|      \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n166|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n167|      \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n168|      \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n169|      \"same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids\": [\"codex_sessions\"]\n170|    },\n171|    \"last_status_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\"\n172|  },\n173|  \"task_board_transaction\": null,\n174|  \"destination_marker_id\": null,\n175|  \"last_error\": null,\n176|  \"started_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:00.000Z\",\n177|  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\",\n178|  \"extensions\": {}\n179|}\n180|~~~\n181|\n182|The two map members above are the normative\n183|<code>MJ-MULTIBLOB-POS</code> fixture: chunk zero for two different blobs is two\n184|independent facts. A flat <code>[0]</code> list is not a valid journal shape.\n185|Crash recovery fixtures are:\n186|\n187|| Fixture | Durable facts after restart | Required recovery |\n188|| --- | --- | --- |\n189|| <code>MJ-CRASH-STAGE</code> | Some per-blob chunk sets, no verified whole blob | Request only absent indexes; never mark another blob's equal index present |\n190|| <code>MJ-RPC-PREPARE-LOST</code> | The destination journal and prepare receipt exist, but the Mesh RPC response was lost | Retry <code>materialize.prepare</code> with the caller-retained operation/materialization IDs and identical body; return the recorded result and create no second journal, authority, replica, plan, or bridge ID |\n191|| <code>MJ-CRASH-PREPARE-LOST</code> | Provider call may have prepared but response was lost | Call <code>materialize-status</code> with the same IDs; persist returned prepared token before any commit/rollback |\n192|| <code>MJ-CRASH-COMMIT-LOST</code> | Journal says committing | Status <code>committed</code> plus exact destination marker commits the journal; prepared rolls back or retries commit; unknown fails closed |\n193|| <code>MJ-CRASH-ROLLBACK-LOST</code> | Journal says rolling_back | Status <code>rolled_back</code> plus restored predecessor closes recovery; prepared retries rollback; unknown fails closed |\n194|| <code>MJ-CRASH-MARKER-MISMATCH</code> | Plugin says committed but destination marker/plan differs | <code>integrity_failure</code>; quarantine transaction and mutate nothing further |\n195|\n196|The following embedded value is the normative\n197|<code>MJ-TASK-BOARD-OPENED-POS</code> fixture. It is persisted in\n198|<code>task_board_transaction</code> before <code>materialize.commit</code>\n199|returns <code>prepared</code>:\n200|\n201|~~~json\n202|{\n203|  \"bundle_id\": \"sha256:0af7b44e7063375a0f06e546fd820438c72607f191c14be78d35c8ffa109844f\",\n204|  \"activation_mode\": \"ownership_transfer\",\n205|  \"import_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a10-71aa-8111-1234567890ab\",\n206|  \"open_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a20-72bb-8222-1234567890ab\",\n207|  \"adopt_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a30-73cc-8333-1234567890ab\",\n208|  \"resume_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a40-74dd-8444-1234567890ab\",\n209|  \"state\": \"opened\",\n210|  \"import_token\": null,\n211|  \"staged_manager_ref\": null,\n212|  \"import_expires_at\": null,\n213|  \"open_token\": \"b3duZXItb25seS1vcGVuLXRva2VuLTAxMjM0NTY3ODlhYmNkZWY\",\n214|  \"dormant_manager_ref\": \"tbm:dormant:0198f4c8-7a10-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n215|  \"open_expires_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:22:10.000Z\",\n216|  \"manager_session_ref\": null,\n217|  \"ax_binding\": null,\n218|  \"last_bridge_state\": \"dormant\",\n219|  \"last_status_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\",\n220|  \"cleanup_state\": \"not_started\",\n221|  \"cleanup_after\": null\n222|}\n223|~~~\n224|\n225|Task-board staging is part of the materialization transaction, not a\n226|precondition performed outside it. The coordinator MUST follow this order for\n227|graceful takeover, force takeover, passive sync, owner resume, and fork:\n228|\n229|1. Before the first call, the caller allocates the materialization and prepare\n230|   operation IDs. <code>materialize.prepare</code> creates the journal by durably\n231|   binding both IDs and the canonical request digest before allocating a fresh\n232|   staging authority or four stable bridge operation IDs and before any bridge\n233|   mutation.\n234|2. Transfer installs and validates the bundle at that authority. The\n235|   coordinator calls bridge <code>import</code>, persists the imported state,\n236|   calls <code>open</code>, and persists the opened state. A passive replica\n237|   stops here; owner activation is forbidden before the applicable lease is\n238|   authoritative.\n239|3. <code>materialize.commit</code> installs all non-task-board authorities and\n240|   returns <code>prepared</code> only after the opened state is durable. A\n241|   task-board-only transaction still uses this commit phase and\n242|   <code>single_root_transaction</code>.\n243|4. For <code>dormant_replica</code>, finalize securely destroys ax's local copy\n244|   of the open token, records <code>dormant_finalized</code>, and leaves the\n245|   manager inert until the bridge's mandatory token/dormant-state expiry; v1\n246|   defines no unlisted bridge invalidation operation. For an owner path, finalize verifies\n247|   the destination lease, calls <code>adopt</code> with the persisted token and\n248|   exact Ax Binding, verifies bridge status, calls <code>resume</code> with the\n249|   persisted profile, verifies running/idle, and only then records\n250|   <code>resumed</code> and commits cleanup.\n251|5. Before successful adopt, rollback uses the stable IDs to query status,\n252|   invalidates or lets expire the staged/dormant state, removes the fresh\n253|   staging authority, and restores every other authority. After successful\n254|   adopt, the manager is active authority: byte rollback is forbidden; recovery\n255|   must fence/stop that manager or finish resume/finalize under the same lease.\n256|\n257|Bridge status plus the journal is the only recovery authority. The following\n258|cases are mandatory:\n259|\n260|| Fixture | Crash/lost response | Recovery |\n261|| --- | --- | --- |\n262|| <code>TB-TXN-IMPORT-LOST</code> | Import may have succeeded; journal is <code>not_started</code> | Retry import with identical operation ID/body; persist the returned identical token/reference or reject <code>idempotency_mismatch</code> |\n263|| <code>TB-TXN-OPEN-LOST</code> | Open may have succeeded; imported facts are durable | Retry open with its stable ID; bridge returns the same dormant reference/token; persist before commit |\n264|| <code>TB-TXN-ADOPT-LOST</code> | Adopt may have succeeded after the lease became authoritative | Query bridge status by dormant/manager reference and exact binding, then retry adopt with the same ID; never import a second manager |\n265|| <code>TB-TXN-RESUME-LOST</code> | Resume may have started provider work | Query status, retry resume only with the same ID/profile, and publish <code>session.resumed</code> once |\n266|| <code>TB-TXN-TOKEN-EXPIRED</code> | Import/open token expired before adopt | Before lease activation, rollback; after lease activation, remain stopped owner and re-run prepare from the same checkpoint with fresh operation IDs |\n267|| <code>TB-TXN-BINDING-MISMATCH</code> | Bridge reports another session/epoch/lease | <code>lease_conflict</code>; preserve evidence and mutate nothing further |\n268|| <code>TB-TXN-PASSIVE</code> | Passive sync reaches opened dormant state | Finalize dormant without adopt/resume; managed replica remains non-executable |\n269|\n270|No flow may call bridge import or open before the corresponding journal exists,\n271|reuse a staging root that contains manager state, inspect private manager state,\n272|or substitute a blank provider session after a missing/expired bundle.\n273|\n274|#### Managed Replica Marker document\n275|\n276|The second recovery-contract variant is an immutable Managed Replica Marker.\n277|It is the authority for classifying a destination as managed; a SQLite row,\n278|directory name, or prior command success without this marker is not authority.\n279|Its closed object contains exactly:\n280|\n281|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n282|| --- | --- | --- |\n283|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Journal schema identifier |\n284|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>2.0.0</code> |\n285|| <code>document_kind</code> | enum | Literal <code>managed_replica_marker</code> |\n286|| <code>marker_id</code> | digest | JCS identity with this field omitted |\n287|| <code>managed_replica_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable identity of one host/path replica across updates |\n288|| <code>host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Host on which the marker is authoritative |\n289|| <code>platform</code> | enum | <code>macos</code>, <code>linux</code>, <code>wsl2</code>, or <code>windows</code> |\n290|| <code>workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Exact materialized group |\n291|| <code>primary_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Session/checkpoint that drove this materialization |\n292|| <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Validated source checkpoint |\n293|| <code>workspace_group_record_id</code> | digest | Unique Section 5.6 topology record |\n294|| <code>workspace_manifest_id</code> | digest | Exact installed workspace-group root manifest |\n295|| <code>plan_id</code> | digest | Executed Materialization Plan |\n296|| <code>materialization_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Journal/RPC transaction that installed it |\n297|| <code>destination</code> | Replica Destination | Closed shape below |\n298|| <code>predecessor_marker_id</code> | digest or null | Prior current marker; null only for a newly managed path |\n299|| <code>committed_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic commit time |\n300|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS machine-local extensions only |\n301|\n302|Replica Destination contains exactly\n303|<code>logical_root:string[1..64]</code>,\n304|<code>workspace_relative_path:path</code>, and\n305|<code>resolved_path_fingerprint:digest</code>. The first two resolve through\n306|the current host configuration. The fingerprint is SHA-256 of the UTF-8 bytes\n307|<code>urn:ax:replica-path:1 NUL platform NUL canonical-absolute-path</code>,\n308|where NUL is one zero byte and Windows path case/volume normalization follows\n309|Section 3.2. It detects remapped configuration; it is routing evidence, not a\n310|logical workspace identity.\n311|\n312|Normative marker fixture:\n313|\n314|~~~json\n315|{\n316|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal\",\n317|  \"schema_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n318|  \"document_kind\": \"managed_replica_marker\",\n319|  \"marker_id\": \"sha256:385c71c7a29a43615c9d35ffb7c93ae20cd9419bbca461627048de575cade94c\",\n320|  \"managed_replica_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-2234567890ab\",\n321|  \"host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n322|  \"platform\": \"linux\",\n323|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n324|  \"primary_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n325|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n326|  \"workspace_group_record_id\": \"sha256:3b366ca989681c63323c5de6db28198796aa913947ad3cd9456fc6dcee62b743\",\n327|  \"workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n328|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n329|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n330|  \"destination\": {\n331|    \"logical_root\": \"relux\",\n332|    \"workspace_relative_path\": \"payments\",\n333|    \"resolved_path_fingerprint\": \"sha256:244d99a3e794e9ea89b4e30429adfd6bc142c069cf0635576e010031f5b85ded\"\n334|  },\n335|  \"predecessor_marker_id\": null,\n336|  \"committed_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:30.000Z\",\n337|  \"extensions\": {}\n338|}\n339|~~~\n340|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c66b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae11-990a-7e72-a802-0a0580c41ec6"},"sequence":400,"recorded_at":1780531400000795,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae12-dfdf-7331-8451-ea9ebb09df68"},"task_id":"01a0ae12-dfdf-7331-8451-ea9ebb09df68","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0ae12-dfdf-7331-8451-ea9ebb09df68"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c66d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae11-990a-7e72-a802-0a0580c41ec6"},"sequence":401,"recorded_at":1780531400000797,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae12dc37763da6a09caebc23f6d7","text":"Read text file `/tmp/rev3k3e6m/spec106.md`.\n1|### 10.6 Materialization Journal\n2|\n3|Materialization Journal schema\n4|<code>urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal</code> version\n5|<code>2.0.0</code> is a two-variant machine-local recovery contract. Both the\n6|mutable journal and immutable managed-replica marker MUST NOT be replicated.\n7|The journal top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n8|\n9|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n10|| --- | --- | --- |\n11|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Journal schema identifier |\n12|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>2.0.0</code> |\n13|| <code>document_kind</code> | enum | Literal <code>journal</code> |\n14|| <code>materialization_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable across retries |\n15|| <code>prepare_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Caller-stable Mesh RPC prepare idempotency key, allocated with the materialization ID before the first request |\n16|| <code>prepare_request_digest</code> | digest | SHA-256 of the complete canonical <code>materialize.prepare</code> request body, including both caller-stable IDs |\n17|| <code>transfer_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null | Null when all inputs already exist locally |\n18|| <code>plan_id</code> | digest | Exact Materialization Plan |\n19|| <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Validated source checkpoint |\n20|| <code>managed_replica_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null | Non-null when workspace bytes participate |\n21|| <code>authority_states</code> | map(root-id,Authority Journal State)[0..512] | Exactly one entry per plan RootAuthority; empty only for validation-only provider plan |\n22|| <code>expected_prior_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for absent/empty destination |\n23|| <code>completed_blob_chunks</code> | map(digest,sorted unique uint32[0..32768])[0..65536] | Chunk indexes keyed by their Blob ID; sufficient for the maximum file/blob cardinality of one committed transfer closure |\n24|| <code>verified_blob_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..65536] | Whole-blob verification, not chunk presence; sufficient for the maximum file/blob cardinality of one committed transfer closure |\n25|| <code>phase</code> | enum | <code>staging</code>, <code>validating</code>, <code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, <code>rolling_back</code>, <code>rolled_back</code>, <code>committed</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n26|| <code>provider_transaction</code> | Provider Journal Transaction or null | Non-null only when a provider plugin participates |\n27|| <code>task_board_transaction</code> | Task-board Journal Transaction or null | Non-null only when the task-board bridge participates |\n28|| <code>destination_marker_id</code> | digest or null | Managed-replica marker; non-null in committed workspace/composite transactions |\n29|| <code>last_error</code> | Structured Error or null | Redacted exact Section 15.1 object |\n30|| <code>started_at</code> | timestamp | First durable journal write |\n31|| <code>updated_at</code> | timestamp | Latest durable transition, not authority |\n32|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS machine-local extensions only |\n33|\n34|Provider Journal Transaction is a closed object containing exactly\n35|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n36|<code>state:unknown|prepared|committed|rolled_back</code>,\n37|<code>rollback_token:base64url-256+|null</code>,\n38|<code>transaction_authority:ProviderTransactionAuthority</code>, and\n39|<code>last_status_at:timestamp</code>. Prepared requires a non-null token;\n40|every other state requires null. The token and transaction root are\n41|machine-local and MUST be redacted from ordinary logs. The authority's\n42|materialization, provider, transaction, and plan IDs MUST equal the journal and\n43|referenced plan; its root is the only path passed to later plugin processes.\n44|\n45|Task-board Journal Transaction is a closed object containing exactly:\n46|\n47|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n48|| --- | --- | --- |\n49|| <code>bundle_id</code> | digest | Exact Task-board Bundle installed by the plan |\n50|| <code>activation_mode</code> | enum | <code>dormant_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, <code>ownership_transfer</code>, or <code>fork</code> |\n51|| <code>import_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge import key allocated before import |\n52|| <code>open_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge open key allocated before open |\n53|| <code>adopt_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge adopt key allocated before adopt |\n54|| <code>resume_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge resume key allocated before resume |\n55|| <code>state</code> | enum | <code>not_started</code>, <code>imported</code>, <code>opened</code>, <code>adopted</code>, <code>resumed</code>, <code>dormant_finalized</code>, <code>rolled_back</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n56|| <code>import_token</code> | base64url-256+ or null | Owner-only bridge token; non-null exactly in <code>imported</code> and consumed by <code>open</code> |\n57|| <code>staged_manager_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null exactly in <code>imported</code> and consumed by <code>open</code> |\n58|| <code>import_expires_at</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null exactly while import token is usable |\n59|| <code>open_token</code> | base64url-256+ or null | Owner-only bridge token; non-null from opened until adopt or dormant finalization |\n60|| <code>dormant_manager_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null in <code>opened</code> and <code>dormant_finalized</code>; consumed and replaced by <code>manager_session_ref</code> on adopt |\n61|| <code>open_expires_at</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null exactly while open token is usable |\n62|| <code>manager_session_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null after successful adopt |\n63|| <code>ax_binding</code> | Ax Binding or null | Non-null after successful adopt |\n64|| <code>last_bridge_state</code> | enum or null | <code>dormant</code>, <code>quiesced</code>, <code>stopped</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>idle</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n65|| <code>last_status_at</code> | timestamp or null | Time of last bridge status reconciliation |\n66|| <code>cleanup_state</code> | enum | <code>not_started</code>, <code>pending_expiry</code>, <code>retained_active</code>, or <code>removed</code> |\n67|| <code>cleanup_after</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null only for dormant finalized state; copied from the last open expiry |\n68|\n69|Ax Binding is the exact closed bridge shape\n70|<code>{ax_session_id:UUIDv7, lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0, lease_id:UUIDv4}</code>.\n71|The four operation IDs are allocated once with the materialization ID and MUST\n72|survive process restart. A retry MUST use the same operation ID and byte-equal\n73|body. Tokens and manager references are local recovery capabilities: they MUST\n74|be encrypted with the platform credential facility when available, owner-only\n75|at rest otherwise, redacted from ordinary logs, excluded from replication, and\n76|never returned by Mesh RPC.\n77|\n78|The null/state invariants are exact. <code>not_started</code> has all tokens and\n79|references null. <code>imported</code> has import token, staged reference, and\n80|import expiry only. <code>opened</code> has open token, dormant reference, and\n81|open expiry only. <code>adopted</code> and <code>resumed</code> have manager\n82|reference and binding only; their cleanup state is\n83|<code>retained_active</code>. <code>dormant_finalized</code> has dormant\n84|reference only, no usable token, bridge state <code>dormant</code>, and cleanup\n85|state <code>pending_expiry</code> with non-null <code>cleanup_after</code> equal\n86|to the consumed open expiry. Every other state requires\n87|<code>cleanup_after = null</code>. <code>rolled_back</code> has no token or\n88|reference and cleanup state <code>removed</code>. <code>failed</code> preserves\n89|only the still-valid token/reference pair needed for deterministic status or\n90|expiry recovery; <code>last_error</code> explains the failure.\n91|\n92|Authority Journal State is a closed object containing exactly\n93|<code>root_path:absolute-path</code>,\n94|<code>completed_sequences:sorted unique uint53[0..65536]</code>,\n95|<code>observed_prior_digest:digest|null</code>,\n96|<code>rollback_root:absolute-path|null</code>, and\n97|<code>state:staging|prepared|committed|rolled_back</code>. The root path MUST\n98|equal its plan authority; completed sequences contain only operations naming\n99|that authority. Prepared requires a non-null rollback root, committed and\n100|rolled-back require null after cleanup, and staging permits null only before\n101|the first target backup exists. The observed prior digest equals every\n102|non-null operation predecessor for a one-target authority; an authority with\n103|multiple distinct predecessors uses null here and each operation backup stores\n104|its own digest under the rollback root. For a provider-store authority, the\n105|rollback root MUST equal\n106|<code>ProviderTransactionAuthority.root_path/backups/&lt;authority-id&gt;</code>;\n107|the host journal references the plugin backup and MUST NOT allocate a second\n108|provider backup location.\n109|\n110|After a crash, <code>ax</code> MUST resume a valid staging transaction or roll\n111|it back. It MUST NOT guess whether an incomplete commit succeeded; it MUST\n112|reconcile the journal, destination marker, and manifest digest.\n113|\n114|Normative example:\n115|\n116|~~~json\n117|{\n118|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal\",\n119|  \"schema_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n120|  \"document_kind\": \"journal\",\n121|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n122|  \"prepare_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-b180-72cc-9271-1234567890ab\",\n123|  \"prepare_request_digest\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\n124|  \"transfer_id\": \"0198f4c8-d3a0-74bb-9475-1234567890ab\",\n125|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n126|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n127|  \"managed_replica_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-2234567890ab\",\n128|  \"authority_states\": {\n129|    \"codex_sessions\": {\n130|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.codex/sessions\",\n131|      \"completed_sequences\": [2],\n132|      \"observed_prior_digest\": null,\n133|      \"rollback_root\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/provider-transactions/codex/0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab/backups/codex_sessions\",\n134|      \"state\": \"prepared\"\n135|    },\n136|    \"workspace_relux\": {\n137|      \"root_path\": \"/srv/relux\",\n138|      \"completed_sequences\": [1],\n139|      \"observed_prior_digest\": \"sha256:3333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333\",\n140|      \"rollback_root\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/materializations/0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab/workspace_relux\",\n141|      \"state\": \"prepared\"\n142|    }\n143|  },\n144|  \"expected_prior_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:2222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222\",\n145|  \"completed_blob_chunks\": {\n146|    \"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\": [0],\n147|    \"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\": [0]\n148|  },\n149|  \"verified_blob_ids\": [\n150|    \"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\",\n151|    \"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\"\n152|  ],\n153|  \"phase\": \"prepared\",\n154|  \"provider_transaction\": {\n155|    \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n156|    \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n157|    \"state\": \"prepared\",\n158|    \"rollback_token\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXowMTIzNDU2Nzg5QUI\",\n159|    \"transaction_authority\": {\n160|      \"authority_id\": \"provider_transaction\",\n161|      \"kind\": \"provider_transaction\",\n162|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/provider-transactions/codex/0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n163|      \"layout\": \"provider_transaction_v1\",\n164|      \"access\": \"read_write\",\n165|      \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n166|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n167|      \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n168|      \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n169|      \"same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids\": [\"codex_sessions\"]\n170|    },\n171|    \"last_status_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\"\n172|  },\n173|  \"task_board_transaction\": null,\n174|  \"destination_marker_id\": null,\n175|  \"last_error\": null,\n176|  \"started_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:00.000Z\",\n177|  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\",\n178|  \"extensions\": {}\n179|}\n180|~~~\n181|\n182|The two map members above are the normative\n183|<code>MJ-MULTIBLOB-POS</code> fixture: chunk zero for two different blobs is two\n184|independent facts. A flat <code>[0]</code> list is not a valid journal shape.\n185|Crash recovery fixtures are:\n186|\n187|| Fixture | Durable facts after restart | Required recovery |\n188|| --- | --- | --- |\n189|| <code>MJ-CRASH-STAGE</code> | Some per-blob chunk sets, no verified whole blob | Request only absent indexes; never mark another blob's equal index present |\n190|| <code>MJ-RPC-PREPARE-LOST</code> | The destination journal and prepare receipt exist, but the Mesh RPC response was lost | Retry <code>materialize.prepare</code> with the caller-retained operation/materialization IDs and identical body; return the recorded result and create no second journal, authority, replica, plan, or bridge ID |\n191|| <code>MJ-CRASH-PREPARE-LOST</code> | Provider call may have prepared but response was lost | Call <code>materialize-status</code> with the same IDs; persist returned prepared token before any commit/rollback |\n192|| <code>MJ-CRASH-COMMIT-LOST</code> | Journal says committing | Status <code>committed</code> plus exact destination marker commits the journal; prepared rolls back or retries commit; unknown fails closed |\n193|| <code>MJ-CRASH-ROLLBACK-LOST</code> | Journal says rolling_back | Status <code>rolled_back</code> plus restored predecessor closes recovery; prepared retries rollback; unknown fails closed |\n194|| <code>MJ-CRASH-MARKER-MISMATCH</code> | Plugin says committed but destination marker/plan differs | <code>integrity_failure</code>; quarantine transaction and mutate nothing further |\n195|\n196|The following embedded value is the normative\n197|<code>MJ-TASK-BOARD-OPENED-POS</code> fixture. It is persisted in\n198|<code>task_board_transaction</code> before <code>materialize.commit</code>\n199|returns <code>prepared</code>:\n200|\n201|~~~json\n202|{\n203|  \"bundle_id\": \"sha256:0af7b44e7063375a0f06e546fd820438c72607f191c14be78d35c8ffa109844f\",\n204|  \"activation_mode\": \"ownership_transfer\",\n205|  \"import_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a10-71aa-8111-1234567890ab\",\n206|  \"open_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a20-72bb-8222-1234567890ab\",\n207|  \"adopt_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a30-73cc-8333-1234567890ab\",\n208|  \"resume_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a40-74dd-8444-1234567890ab\",\n209|  \"state\": \"opened\",\n210|  \"import_token\": null,\n211|  \"staged_manager_ref\": null,\n212|  \"import_expires_at\": null,\n213|  \"open_token\": \"b3duZXItb25seS1vcGVuLXRva2VuLTAxMjM0NTY3ODlhYmNkZWY\",\n214|  \"dormant_manager_ref\": \"tbm:dormant:0198f4c8-7a10-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n215|  \"open_expires_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:22:10.000Z\",\n216|  \"manager_session_ref\": null,\n217|  \"ax_binding\": null,\n218|  \"last_bridge_state\": \"dormant\",\n219|  \"last_status_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\",\n220|  \"cleanup_state\": \"not_started\",\n221|  \"cleanup_after\": null\n222|}\n223|~~~\n224|\n225|Task-board staging is part of the materialization transaction, not a\n226|precondition performed outside it. The coordinator MUST follow this order for\n227|graceful takeover, force takeover, passive sync, owner resume, and fork:\n228|\n229|1. Before the first call, the caller allocates the materialization and prepare\n230|   operation IDs. <code>materialize.prepare</code> creates the journal by durably\n231|   binding both IDs and the canonical request digest before allocating a fresh\n232|   staging authority or four stable bridge operation IDs and before any bridge\n233|   mutation.\n234|2. Transfer installs and validates the bundle at that authority. The\n235|   coordinator calls bridge <code>import</code>, persists the imported state,\n236|   calls <code>open</code>, and persists the opened state. A passive replica\n237|   stops here; owner activation is forbidden before the applicable lease is\n238|   authoritative.\n239|3. <code>materialize.commit</code> installs all non-task-board authorities and\n240|   returns <code>prepared</code> only after the opened state is durable. A\n241|   task-board-only transaction still uses this commit phase and\n242|   <code>single_root_transaction</code>.\n243|4. For <code>dormant_replica</code>, finalize securely destroys ax's local copy\n244|   of the open token, records <code>dormant_finalized</code>, and leaves the\n245|   manager inert until the bridge's mandatory token/dormant-state expiry; v1\n246|   defines no unlisted bridge invalidation operation. For an owner path, finalize verifies\n247|   the destination lease, calls <code>adopt</code> with the persisted token and\n248|   exact Ax Binding, verifies bridge status, calls <code>resume</code> with the\n249|   persisted profile, verifies running/idle, and only then records\n250|   <code>resumed</code> and commits cleanup.\n251|5. Before successful adopt, rollback uses the stable IDs to query status,\n252|   invalidates or lets expire the staged/dormant state, removes the fresh\n253|   staging authority, and restores every other authority. After successful\n254|   adopt, the manager is active authority: byte rollback is forbidden; recovery\n255|   must fence/stop that manager or finish resume/finalize under the same lease.\n256|\n257|Bridge status plus the journal is the only recovery authority. The following\n258|cases are mandatory:\n259|\n260|| Fixture | Crash/lost response | Recovery |\n261|| --- | --- | --- |\n262|| <code>TB-TXN-IMPORT-LOST</code> | Import may have succeeded; journal is <code>not_started</code> | Retry import with identical operation ID/body; persist the returned identical token/reference or reject <code>idempotency_mismatch</code> |\n263|| <code>TB-TXN-OPEN-LOST</code> | Open may have succeeded; imported facts are durable | Retry open with its stable ID; bridge returns the same dormant reference/token; persist before commit |\n264|| <code>TB-TXN-ADOPT-LOST</code> | Adopt may have succeeded after the lease became authoritative | Query bridge status by dormant/manager reference and exact binding, then retry adopt with the same ID; never import a second manager |\n265|| <code>TB-TXN-RESUME-LOST</code> | Resume may have started provider work | Query status, retry resume only with the same ID/profile, and publish <code>session.resumed</code> once |\n266|| <code>TB-TXN-TOKEN-EXPIRED</code> | Import/open token expired before adopt | Before lease activation, rollback; after lease activation, remain stopped owner and re-run prepare from the same checkpoint with fresh operation IDs |\n267|| <code>TB-TXN-BINDING-MISMATCH</code> | Bridge reports another session/epoch/lease | <code>lease_conflict</code>; preserve evidence and mutate nothing further |\n268|| <code>TB-TXN-PASSIVE</code> | Passive sync reaches opened dormant state | Finalize dormant without adopt/resume; managed replica remains non-executable |\n269|\n270|No flow may call bridge import or open before the corresponding journal exists,\n271|reuse a staging root that contains manager state, inspect private manager state,\n272|or substitute a blank provider session after a missing/expired bundle.\n273|\n274|#### Managed Replica Marker document\n275|\n276|The second recovery-contract variant is an immutable Managed Replica Marker.\n277|It is the authority for classifying a destination as managed; a SQLite row,\n278|directory name, or prior command success without this marker is not authority.\n279|Its closed object contains exactly:\n280|\n281|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n282|| --- | --- | --- |\n283|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Journal schema identifier |\n284|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>2.0.0</code> |\n285|| <code>document_kind</code> | enum | Literal <code>managed_replica_marker</code> |\n286|| <code>marker_id</code> | digest | JCS identity with this field omitted |\n287|| <code>managed_replica_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable identity of one host/path replica across updates |\n288|| <code>host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Host on which the marker is authoritative |\n289|| <code>platform</code> | enum | <code>macos</code>, <code>linux</code>, <code>wsl2</code>, or <code>windows</code> |\n290|| <code>workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Exact materialized group |\n291|| <code>primary_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Session/checkpoint that drove this materialization |\n292|| <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Validated source checkpoint |\n293|| <code>workspace_group_record_id</code> | digest | Unique Section 5.6 topology record |\n294|| <code>workspace_manifest_id</code> | digest | Exact installed workspace-group root manifest |\n295|| <code>plan_id</code> | digest | Executed Materialization Plan |\n296|| <code>materialization_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Journal/RPC transaction that installed it |\n297|| <code>destination</code> | Replica Destination | Closed shape below |\n298|| <code>predecessor_marker_id</code> | digest or null | Prior current marker; null only for a newly managed path |\n299|| <code>committed_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic commit time |\n300|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS machine-local extensions only |\n301|\n302|Replica Destination contains exactly\n303|<code>logical_root:string[1..64]</code>,\n304|<code>workspace_relative_path:path</code>, and\n305|<code>resolved_path_fingerprint:digest</code>. The first two resolve through\n306|the current host configuration. The fingerprint is SHA-256 of the UTF-8 bytes\n307|<code>urn:ax:replica-path:1 NUL platform NUL canonical-absolute-path</code>,\n308|where NUL is one zero byte and Windows path case/volume normalization follows\n309|Section 3.2. It detects remapped configuration; it is routing evidence, not a\n310|logical workspace identity.\n311|\n312|Normative marker fixture:\n313|\n314|~~~json\n315|{\n316|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal\",\n317|  \"schema_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n318|  \"document_kind\": \"managed_replica_marker\",\n319|  \"marker_id\": \"sha256:385c71c7a29a43615c9d35ffb7c93ae20cd9419bbca461627048de575cade94c\",\n320|  \"managed_replica_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-2234567890ab\",\n321|  \"host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n322|  \"platform\": \"linux\",\n323|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n324|  \"primary_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n325|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n326|  \"workspace_group_record_id\": \"sha256:3b366ca989681c63323c5de6db28198796aa913947ad3cd9456fc6dcee62b743\",\n327|  \"workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n328|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n329|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n330|  \"destination\": {\n331|    \"logical_root\": \"relux\",\n332|    \"workspace_relative_path\": \"payments\",\n333|    \"resolved_path_fingerprint\": \"sha256:244d99a3e794e9ea89b4e30429adfd6bc142c069cf0635576e010031f5b85ded\"\n334|  },\n335|  \"predecessor_marker_id\": null,\n336|  \"committed_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:30.000Z\",\n337|  \"extensions\": {}\n338|}\n339|~~~\n340|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
