{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c69b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae11-990a-7e72-a802-0a0580c41ec6"},"sequence":424,"recorded_at":1780531400000843,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"46e4ecbd-d202-41f9-9d18-3e98ef6b52fc"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae12-e76b-7b52-80b3-22d14f8d7e51"},"task_id":"01a0ae12-e76b-7b52-80b3-22d14f8d7e51","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae12-e76b-7b52-80b3-22d14f8d7e51","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev3k3e6m/spec106.md`.\n(339 line(s) above)\n340|\n341|The marker is stored as owner-only JSON in both\n342|<code>&lt;state&gt;/managed-replicas/&lt;managed-replica-id&gt;/markers/sha256/HH/REST.json</code>,\n343|using <code>digest_path_v1(marker_id)</code> from Section 3.2,\n344|and the atomically replaceable\n345|<code>&lt;state&gt;/managed-replicas/&lt;managed-replica-id&gt;/current.json</code>.\n346|The history file is create-new, fsynced, and never changed. The writer then\n347|writes a same-directory temporary current file, fsyncs it, atomically renames\n348|it, and fsyncs the parent where supported. The journal records the marker ID\n349|only after the target bytes and history file are durable. SQLite indexes these\n350|files and MUST be rebuildable by scanning them.\n351|\n352|A current marker is valid only when its self-ID, predecessor chain, host ID,\n353|platform, workspace group and topology record, source checkpoint, plan,\n354|materialization, configured logical-root resolution, and path fingerprint all\n355|validate. A marker copied from another host or placed under another managed-\n356|replica directory is never destination authority.\n357|\n358|For crash recovery, a <code>committing</code> journal with no current marker may\n359|create the exact marker only after revalidating every plan authority,\n360|predecessor, installed manifest byte, provider transaction, and task-board\n361|state. Any mismatch rolls back when possible or fails integrity-closed; it\n362|never writes a marker merely because the target path exists. A current marker\n363|whose plan/checkpoint/materialization differs from the journal is\n364|<code>MJ-CRASH-MARKER-MISMATCH</code>.\n365|\n366|Destination classification is deterministic:\n367|\n368|| Durable state | Classification/action |\n369|| --- | --- |\n370|| No marker; target absent | <code>absent</code> |\n371|| No marker; target empty | <code>empty</code> |\n372|| No marker; target nonempty | <code>unmanaged_nonempty</code> |\n373|| Valid current marker resolves to this exact path and a fresh workspace capture equals <code>workspace_manifest_id</code> | <code>managed_unchanged</code> |\n374|| Valid current marker resolves here but fresh content differs | <code>managed_divergent</code>; preserve both states |\n375|| Marker digest, path fingerprint, predecessor chain, or referenced object is invalid | <code>integrity_failure</code>; report managed divergence diagnostically and mutate nothing |\n376|\n377|<code>MARKER-ABSENT</code>, <code>MARKER-MATCH</code>,\n378|<code>MARKER-CONTENT-MISMATCH</code>, <code>MARKER-PATH-MISMATCH</code>, and\n379|<code>MARKER-CRASH-RECONSTRUCT</code> are the five rows above plus the\n380|crash-reconstruction rule and are normative fixtures. A reader that does not\n381|support this major version MUST treat the path as managed-but-incompatible and\n382|fail closed; migration follows Section 17 and MUST write a new marker linked\n383|through <code>predecessor_marker_id</code>, never edit an old marker.\n384|\n385|### 10.7 Tombstone\n386|\n387|Tombstone schema <code>urn:ax:schema:tombstone</code> version\n388|<code>1.0.0</code> is immutable. Its common closed shape is:\n389|\n390|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n391|| --- | --- | --- |\n392|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Tombstone schema identifier |\n393|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n394|| <code>tombstone_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n395|| <code>scope</code> | enum | <code>session</code>, <code>workspace_entry</code>, <code>provider_snapshot</code>, or <code>managed_replica</code> |\n396|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Scope subject defined below |\n397|| <code>authorizing_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Session whose owner authorizes the action |\n398|| <code>basis_event_id</code> | digest | Immediately preceding authoritative event for the authorizing lease |\n399|| <code>lease_epoch</code> | uint53 | Authorizing lease epoch |\n400|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Authorizing fencing token |\n401|| <code>target</code> | tagged object | Exact scope-specific shape below |\n402|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | MUST equal the authorizing lease holder |\n403|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n404|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n405|\n406|The <code>target</code> object is selected by <code>scope</code> and begins with\n407|an equal <code>kind</code>. It contains exactly:\n408|\n409|| Scope | <code>subject_id</code> | Exact target members after <code>kind</code> |\n410|| --- | --- | --- |\n411|| <code>session</code> | Session ID | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>predecessor_checkpoint_id:digest</code> |\n412|| <code>workspace_entry</code> | Workspace Group ID | <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>predecessor_manifest_id:digest</code>, <code>relative_path:path</code>, <code>entry_type:directory&#124;file&#124;symlink&#124;hardlink</code>, <code>predecessor_entry_digest:digest</code> |\n413|| <code>provider_snapshot</code> | Session ID | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, <code>predecessor_manifest_id:digest</code> |\n414|| <code>managed_replica</code> | Workspace Group ID | <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>managed_replica_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>logical_root:string[1..64]</code>, <code>destination_relative_path:path</code>, <code>predecessor_marker_id:digest</code>, <code>predecessor_checkpoint_id:digest</code> |\n415|\n416|Positive embedded target fixtures for the three variants not used by the full\n417|example are:\n418|\n419|~~~json\n420|{\"kind\":\"session\",\"session_id\":\"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\"session_record_id\":\"sha256:d61701066a7f5dd37bf35fea0e85e7f154251355ad24a49976532d7f79ddc772\",\"predecessor_checkpoint_id\":\"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\"}\n421|~~~\n422|\n423|~~~json\n424|{\"kind\":\"provider_snapshot\",\"session_id\":\"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\"provider_identity_record_id\":\"sha256:c879d766da67a8cfb3a3f6eae2234faa5d52d8df987496eae2218f40e5e220c2\",\"predecessor_manifest_id\":\"sha256:1e817955dcc529e282ab31f91c99561d03b3c5642282d2e0a0e05b0f60dd0f91\"}\n425|~~~\n426|\n427|~~~json\n428|{\"kind\":\"managed_replica\",\"workspace_group_id\":\"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\"target_host_id\":\"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\"managed_replica_id\":\"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-2234567890ab\",\"logical_root\":\"relux\",\"destination_relative_path\":\"replicas/payments\",\"predecessor_marker_id\":\"sha256:385c71c7a29a43615c9d35ffb7c93ae20cd9419bbca461627048de575cade94c\",\"predecessor_checkpoint_id\":\"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\"}\n429|~~~\n430|\n431|Repeated IDs in the target MUST equal the corresponding common/session/group\n432|records. A workspace-entry <code>workspace_id</code> MUST name one member of the\n433|group, its predecessor MUST be that member's <code>workspace_tree</code>\n434|manifest, and its path is member-relative. An entry digest is SHA-256 of the\n435|JCS bytes of the complete Transfer Manifest entry object. A workspace-entry\n436|path names exactly one entry in that predecessor; a\n437|directory target MUST be empty after separately authorized descendant\n438|deletions. A managed-replica path is relative to one configured logical root\n439|and MUST NOT be empty or that root itself.\n440|\n441|~~~json\n442|{\n443|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:tombstone\",\n444|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n445|  \"tombstone_id\": \"sha256:4acc50a49a714543ef415ab1d68bb605ee825cae2b36308e669f6cfe74f73b3e\",\n446|  \"scope\": \"workspace_entry\",\n447|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n448|  \"authorizing_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n449|  \"basis_event_id\": \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\",\n450|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n451|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n452|  \"target\": {\n453|    \"kind\": \"workspace_entry\",\n454|    \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n455|    \"workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n456|    \"predecessor_manifest_id\": \"sha256:88d93f20f978b92e75d35e67ebd5a41b90ff1afe106363b05c0f7b08614eb4cf\",\n457|    \"relative_path\": \"README.md\",\n458|    \"entry_type\": \"file\",\n459|    \"predecessor_entry_digest\": \"sha256:499419072e3173e840befc74fdc1d334b33bd9a3a03076a08fb792ea9ae264f1\"\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
