on\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Capture durably installs Section 5.4 checkpoint records with attested identities, idempotent replays, and head-bound admission; restore behaviour is not implemented and no clause of Section 5.4 is enumerated.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:5.5\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"validateProviderIdentityRecord\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"core-record-identity-validation\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"validateProviderIdentityRecord validates the Section 5.5 provider identity shape; the host-side destination-adapter read and carry of that record is additionally implemented in internal/provhost CheckIdentity (see the Section 7.6 and Section 7.7 bindings), and no clause of Section 5.5 is enumerated against an acceptance case.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:5.6\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"validateWorkspaceGroupRecord\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n=== 10.6 binding ===\\n        \\\"section:10.6\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/matjournal/store.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Create\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"materialization-journal-lifecycle\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Create durably installs Section 10.6 materialization journals with phase transitions, receipts, and input digests; provider, bridge, and replica effects stay modeled and no clause of Section 10.6 is enumerated.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:11.2\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ForRelease\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.2; no clause of 11.2 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 5 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:11.3\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ForRelease\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.3; no clause of 11.3 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 27 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:11.8\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ForRelease\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.8; no clause of 11.8 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim 