log/cmd/cataloggen/main_test.go:240:\\tif len(fields) != 9 || strings.Join(fields[:3], \\\" \\\") != \\\"go run ./cmd/cataloggen\\\" {\\n./LOGBOOK.md:1023:- ROOT CAUSE: **a clause was claimed against a topically related section instead of against the actor its MUST binds.** Ownership clause `15.1#6` at SPEC.md:11047 was discharged by `LocalFromUntrusted`. That line's only RFC 2119 sentence is \\\"The plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2\\\" - it binds the **provider plugin**, a child process this repository does not build; its only binaries are `cataloggen` and `tracecheck`. The host half of the same table row, which `LocalFromUntrusted` does implement, carries no RFC 2119 keyword at all, so it is not what the clause scanner measured.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:1102:- EVIDENCE: `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 15.2` exited **0**. §15.2 is the nineteen-row normative exit-code registry (SPEC.md:11073-11095) and nothing in the tree implements it — the only `os.Exit` calls are the `exit(1)` paths of `cataloggen` and `tracecheck`. Same for `-section 7.3`, the closed Provider Manifest, whose sole trace is a catalog row naming its URN. Both were bound to `internal/catalog/catalog.go:ForRelease`, an unrelated symbol.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:1192:- STATUS: `internal/canonicaljson` 97.2% before and after, verified against a `git archive HEAD` baseline. gofmt, `go build ./...`, both cross-compile targets, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./... -count=1`, `-cover -count=1`, `-race -count=1`, tracecheck, `cataloggen -check` and all five fuzz gates at 100x exit 0.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:1204:- STATUS: `internal/localstore` unchanged at 86.6%, 90 top-level tests and 130 subtests — this round added assertions to existing cases, not new cases. gofmt, `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./... -count=1`, `-race -count=1`, `-cover -count=1`, both cross-compile targets, global tracecheck, `cataloggen -check` and `git diff --check` all exit 0.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:1473:full and scoped `tracecheck` and `cataloggen -check` — reproduced here at exit\\n===\\ninternal/cigate/targets.go\\ninternal/cigate/claims.go\\ninternal/cigate/targets_test.go\\ninternal/cigate/contracts.go\\ninternal/cigate/claims_test.go\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2736,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 684,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
